d1-2B for LiteRT

The LiteRT graphs (*.tflite and npu/sm8850/*.tflite) and the table (tables/embed_table.npy) in this repository are
converted from LiquidAI/d1-2B, revision 10e7671d44e4b37700020b1eed3f594c5f2af0b4 (https://huggingface.co/LiquidAI/d1-2B),
by Liquid AI. d1-2B is built on LiquidAI/LFM3-VL-2B (https://huggingface.co/LiquidAI/LFM3-VL-2B). Both are licensed
under the LFM Open License v1.0; LICENSE is a copy of the d1-2B repository's LICENSE file. Every graph and the table are
derived from that repository's model.safetensors: the changes are listed under "Changes from the original work" in
README.md and in REPRODUCE.md. The files in npu/sm8850/ were compiled ahead of time from this repository's decision
graphs for the Qualcomm SM8850 with ai-edge-litert 2.2.0 and Qualcomm AI Runtime (QAIRT) 2.47.0.

provider/ holds files of the d1-2B repository at the revision above, unchanged: 12 Python modules, config.json,
tokenizer.json, tokenizer_config.json, calibration.json, chat_template.jinja and processor_config.json (LFM Open License
v1.0).

The Python host (host/) imports the modules of the provider (Liquid AI's model code in the d1-2B repository) that need
no PyTorch and ports, as numpy code, the rest of the d1-2B repository's request handling (runner.py, attention.py,
pointer.py, the readout tables of prompt.py and the picture path of media.py) and its picture preprocessing
(processing_lfm3_vl.py and image_processing_lfm3_vl.py, which run on transformers' TorchvisionBackend, Apache License
2.0), including PyTorch's uint8 antialiased bicubic resize (BSD 3-Clause License). Its tokenizer runs on the tokenizers
library (Apache License 2.0). The conversion scripts (conversion/) run the d1-2B repository's model code with
transformers, litert-torch, ai-edge-quantizer and LiteRT (ai-edge-litert), each licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
The NPU step (conversion/npu/) also needs Qualcomm AI Runtime (QAIRT) 2.47.0, Qualcomm's SDK under its own
license, which is not in this repository.

fixtures/ lists 526 test and control requests (fixtures/requests_public.json). 303 are included with their text: 144 are
SemIf authored144 records (github.com/TheoLeeCJ/SemIf, commit ca3ba65f), Copyright (c) 2026 TheoLeeCJ, licensed under
the MIT License (fixtures/LICENSE-SemIf-MIT.txt); 7 are the example requests of the d1-2B and d1-3B model cards; 152 were
written for these conversions, some over the texts of those examples. 223 are listed by reference only (file, tag, line and SHA-256): 220 records of the transfer-v4
development file of github.com/jaredpalmer/kev at tag kev-1.0 (Apache License 2.0) and 3 made from them. Their text comes
from public datasets under their own licenses and is not included; fixtures/rebuild_requests.py restores it from that
file. fixtures/media/ holds 5 photographs from Wikimedia Commons (CC0 1.0) and 18 synthetic pictures drawn for these
conversions. The photo of the card's picture example (COCO val2017 000000039769.jpg) is not included: the fixtures and the
example give its URL and SHA-256.

